From: zhangtingan <zhangtingan@uniontech.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:50:00 +0800
Subject: Add slice param of vaapi-hevc

Add num_entry_point_offsets field assignment to the VASliceParameterBufferHEVC
structure initialization in vaapi_hevc_decode_slice(). This passes the entry
point offset count to the VAAPI HEVC hardware decoder, improving compatibility
with HEVC streams that use multiple entry points (e.g. WPP parallel encoding).

Port from V20 release/eagle branch (upstream commit df88b4ca,
Change-Id: Ie812214e541641df2f668e82c0e26cad3aaa0f16).
---
 libavcodec/vaapi_hevc.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/libavcodec/vaapi_hevc.c b/libavcodec/vaapi_hevc.c
index 9d668eb55e..cece7a3c3b 100644
--- a/libavcodec/vaapi_hevc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/vaapi_hevc.c
@@ -498,6 +498,7 @@ static int vaapi_hevc_decode_slice(AVCodecContext *avctx,
         .num_ref_idx_l0_active_minus1  = sh->nb_refs[L0] ? sh->nb_refs[L0] - 1 : 0,
         .num_ref_idx_l1_active_minus1  = sh->nb_refs[L1] ? sh->nb_refs[L1] - 1 : 0,
 
+        .num_entry_point_offsets       = sh->num_entry_point_offsets,
+
         .LongSliceFlags.fields = {
             .dependent_slice_segment_flag                 = sh->dependent_slice_segment_flag,
